THOUGHT: The NullAway error is because `batch` is annotated @Nullable but dereferenced unconditionally in `update()`. The safest fix is to guard the call with a null check, which matches how other nullable fields are typically handled and avoids changing behavior beyond skipping rendering when no batch is set. I’ll edit the file to add `if (batch != null)` around `batch.draw(renderData);` and then run the NullAway build to confirm the error count decreases by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '42,46s/  public void update() {
    batch.draw(renderData);
  }
/  public void update() {
    if (batch != null) {
      batch.draw(renderData);
    }
  }
/' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/graphics/g3d/particles/renderers/ParticleControllerRenderer.java && ./gradlew gdx:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -E "NullAway:|error\(s\)\ from\ NullAway" -n new_build_output.log | tail
```

